Coverage (the web RouteAnnouncer.test.tsx contract reproduced natively):
  * no announce on first paint (first-render guard)
  * announces the page title after a navigation, DEFERRING the read (delayMs schedule)
  * empty title clears the live region (web setMessage(''))
  * two consecutive routes with the same title BOTH announce (rotating zero-width-space de-dupe)
  * a second navigation CANCELS the pending read → only the final destination is announced
  * custom delayMs is honoured (0.1s default, 0.5s override)
  * each announcement is voiced to the assistive technology exactly once (polite)
  * projection across loading / empty / error / data + most-recent-first ordering
  * connection axis: stale one-shot auto-refresh (re-arms after live) + offline keeps cache
  * RouteLocationPublisher (useLocation port) + LiveRouteAnnouncerSource end-to-end wiring
  * accessibility label presence (live region + history row) + i18n keys resolve non-empty

